## English

*Last updated: [insert date]*

This policy describes what data TMG collects, how it is used, and how to
request its deletion. It applies to anyone hosting an instance of the bot
(the "operator") and to the Discord servers it's installed on.

### Data controller

The data controller is **whoever hosts the bot instance** (the operator
of the server or infrastructure TMG runs on) — not the original authors
of the open-source code. If you're distributing TMG to your users, fill
in your own contact details here:

- Name/Organization: **[fill in]**
- Contact: **[fill in email]**

### Data we collect

TMG only collects what it needs to function as a moderation bot:

| Data | Source | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Server (guild) ID | Discord | Match settings to the right server |
| Configured channel and role IDs | `/set-log-channel`, `/set-welcome`, `/set-mute-role` commands, or the dashboard | Know where to send logs and welcome messages |
| User ID, moderator ID, reason | `/warn` command | Keep a record of warnings |
| Username, ID, avatar, server list | "Login with Discord" (OAuth2, `identify guilds` scope) | Show only the servers you can manage in the dashboard |

**TMG does not store message content.** When a message is deleted or
edited, its text is forwarded once to the log channel you configured
(it stays inside Discord) — it is not written to the bot's database. The
bot does not read or retain direct messages (DMs).

### Where data is stored

Server settings and warnings are stored in a local SQLite database on
the machine running the bot — nothing is sent to third parties beyond
Discord itself. The access token created when you log into the dashboard
is kept in an encrypted session cookie in your browser, not on a server.

### Who we share it with

- **Discord Inc.**, as the platform the bot operates on (unavoidable for
  any Discord bot).
- **[The hosting provider chosen by the operator]**, if the operator runs
  the bot and database on an external cloud service.

No data is sold or shared for advertising purposes.

### How long we keep it

A server's data is kept for as long as the bot remains in that server.
**When TMG is removed from a server, its settings and related warnings
are automatically deleted.** You can also request earlier deletion by
contacting the address listed above.

### Your rights

If you are in the European Union, the GDPR gives you the right to access
your data, request corrections, deletion, restriction of processing, or
data portability, and the right to lodge a complaint with your national
data protection authority. To exercise these rights, contact the address
above.

### Children

Discord requires users to be at least 13 (or the higher age required in
your country) to use the platform; TMG does not knowingly collect data
from users who don't meet this requirement.

### Changes to this policy

The operator may update this document; the date at the top reflects the
latest revision. Continued use of the bot after a change means you
accept the updated version.
